  "statement_contract": {
    "rule": "One joined statement per distinct eligible key batch; nested target and pivot branches each batch their complete collections under the shared depth/fetched/attachment budget. One attached link consumes two values. Each morph inverse filters its discriminator group before batching. Empty eligible key sets send zero statements; EXISTS adds zero extra statements.",
    "assertions": [
      {
        "operation": "Query, two parents, batch size one, target branch and pivot branch",
        "statements": 5
      },
      {
        "operation": "Explicit Load of three parents with shared targets, target and pivot branches",
        "statements": 3
      },
      {
        "operation": "LoadMissing of already-loaded slots, including empty",
        "statements": 0
      },
      {
        "operation": "Locked source query plus pivot branch inside transaction",
        "statements": 2
      },
      {
        "operation": "Two eligible concrete morph target groups",
        "statements": 2
      },
      {
        "operation": "Empty parent sets or ineligible/NULL morph keys",
        "statements": 0
      },
      {
        "operation": "Each joined existence query",
        "statements": 1,
        "extra_relation_statements": 0
      }
    ]
  },
  "coverage": [
    "16 old/new golden SQL/binding scenarios: pivot constraints and combined order, both nested sides, many/one through, latest/oldest/custom one-of-many and through choice, all morph variants, joined EXISTS/NOT EXISTS.",
    "Public in-memory driver: exact statement counts, close-before-next-statement, shared targets, distinct pivots, loaded-empty preservation, transaction/locked execution and empty eligibility.",
    "Faults: repeated pivot primary returns database.TooManyRows; mismatched target key, decode failure, shared attachment budget, duplicate ordering, depth and empty OfMany fail without partial parents; invalid morph name sends zero SQL.",
    "PostgreSQL source: pivot payloads, duplicate pivot rows, null and missing targets, soft-deleted pivots and pivot visibility, nested batch counts, many/one through, one-of-many ties and soft-deleted targets, all morph kinds and empty groups, nested existence and non-unique target-key TooManyRows."
  ],
